In article <75200@netnews.upenn.edu> decoteau@eniac.seas.upenn.edu (Gary R DeCoteau) writes:

>      I am new to NetHack (level 5 Barbarian).  Somehow, I got
>  a ball & chain attached to my leg --- it's weighing me down.
>  How can I take it off?
>
>      Also, which corpses, besides human, can my Barbarian eat?
>
>      Where can I learn spells?  

Okay, Gary, spoilers ahead, by degree:  minor, major, and total.



Minor:

Did you read something?  Have you got something to read?

That depends.

From the right books.



Major

You read a scroll of punishment.  There is another scroll that will get rid
of the damn thing.

You can eat most corpses.  I would not advise eating human corpses.

Little "+" marks on the screen are usually spellbooks.



Total

A scroll of punishment puts the ball-and-chain on your leg.  (You should have 
been given the message, "You are being punished for your misbehavior.")  It 
can be gotten rid of with a scroll of remove curse.  In the meanwhile, it makes
a pretty good weapon -- but don't throw it at anything more than 2 spaces away!

You can eat any corpse, as long as it's fresh, except for certain that are
poisonous.  Generally, these are the same that have poison attacks.  Mummy,
zombie, and lich corpses are _never_ fresh.  Also:  eating certain corpses gives
you an "intrinsic," or a chance at it.  Thus, for example, eating a dead 
floating eye gives you the "intrinsic" of telepathy.

About spellbooks:  each color/type gives a different spell.  Be careful reading
them; there's a chance of failing to learn the spell, in which case any of 
several things can happen, some of which are fatal to low-level characters.
I recommend dropping all your gold before reading an unknown spellbook.
If you learn a new spell, you will get the message "you add the spell to your
repertoire," but it won't tell you _what_ the spell is.  Use the "x" command to
find out what spells you know; it doesn't take any time (like "i" and "/").

Good luck and happy hacking!


